From: Erbium emulation <roman@nekko.ai>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] spi: cadence-quadspi: fall back to PIO when no PM firmware drives the Versal OSPI DMA mux

zynqmp_pm_ospi_mux_select() returns -ENODEV when CONFIG_ZYNQMP_FIRMWARE
is off or no TF-A is present (e.g. QEMU xlnx-versal-virt). Instead of
failing every read larger than 3 bytes, disable the DMA path and use
indirect PIO reads.
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c
@@ -868,6 +868,16 @@
 		goto nondmard;
 
 	ret = zynqmp_pm_ospi_mux_select(cqspi->pd_dev_id, PM_OSPI_MUX_SEL_DMA);
+	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -EOPNOTSUPP) {
+		/*
+		 * No platform management firmware to steer the OSPI DMA mux
+		 * (e.g. running under QEMU or without TF-A).  Fall back to
+		 * PIO indirect reads for good.
+		 */
+		dev_info_once(dev, "no PM firmware for OSPI DMA, using PIO\n");
+		cqspi->use_dma_read = false;
+		return cqspi_indirect_read_execute(f_pdata, rxbuf, from_addr, n_rx);
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
